\title{Max Margin Interval Tree Changepoint Learner}
\description{
Learns a penalty function for changepoint detection from weak labels via a
max margin interval tree, \code{\link[mmit:mmit]{mmit::mmit()}}.

At train time, each sequence is summarized into a numeric feature vector and
the labels are converted into an interval of admissible \code{log(lambda)}
penalties (the segment path is fitted per sequence, scored against the label
regions, and the error curve inverted). The tree fits these interval targets
directly with a hinge loss, so unlike \link{mlr_learners_changepoint.intregrcv} it
also trains when no label gives a finite lower (or upper) penalty limit.

At predict time, the learner returns \code{response}, the predicted \code{log(lambda)}
per sequence.

The label solvers are chosen by the task's \code{label_type}:
\code{"changepoint"} uses \code{\link[changepoint:cpt.mean]{changepoint::cpt.mean()}}, \code{"peak"} uses
\code{\link[PeakSegOptimal:PeakSegPDPAchrom]{PeakSegOptimal::PeakSegPDPAchrom()}}.

The 'mmit' package is not on CRAN; install it from GitHub with
\code{pak::pak("aldro61/mmit/Rpackage")}.
}
